Subject: Minutes, register and ROC calendar for 2026–27

Dear Mrunal,

Thank you for the minutes book, the register and your tracker. One filing first, then our points before the Board meets on 18 May.

MSME-1 for October to March: Mahesh’s mail of 26 April looked only at micro suppliers. Kudalwadi, a small enterprise, was owed ₹14,36,705 beyond 45 days at 31 March, and Shirur ₹44,660 once its stale cheque was written back. {msme}

Disclosures: the minutes of 19 May 2026 record MBP-1 from three directors, not from Nandini Krishnamurthy. {mbp1}

Minutes: the 12 November minutes went into the book on 24 December, 42 days after the meeting. {minutes}

Borrowing: the renewal of the ₹18 crore cash-credit limit was approved by circular resolution on 22 December. {borrowing}

Register: the MBP-4 entry for Sejal Joglekar’s design contract shows ₹60,000, but the Board approved ₹6,00,000 on 12 November. {register}

